# Product images and 3D models. Log in first (requests/auth.http).
# Uploads are multipart/form-data. With curl (PowerShell: use curl.exe):
#
#   curl.exe -b cookies.txt -F "file=@front.jpg" -F "alt_text=Front view" ^
#     http://localhost:5050/v1/companies/<companyId>/products/<productId>/images
#   curl.exe -b cookies.txt -X PUT -F "file=@chair.glb" ^
#     http://localhost:5050/v1/companies/<companyId>/products/<productId>/model
#
# Images: JPEG/PNG/WebP up to 10 MB, 20 per product. Model: one GLB up to 50 MB.
# The file type is detected from the bytes, not the file name.

@base = http://localhost:5050
@companyId = paste-company-id-here
@productId = paste-product-id-here
@mediaId = paste-media-id-here

### Gallery, model and material check
GET {{base}}/v1/companies/{{companyId}}/products/{{productId}}/media

### Upload an image (REST Client multipart syntax)
POST {{base}}/v1/companies/{{companyId}}/products/{{productId}}/images
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="alt_text"

Front view
--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="front.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./front.png
--BOUNDARY--

### Make an image primary / edit alt text / reorder
PATCH {{base}}/v1/companies/{{companyId}}/products/{{productId}}/images/{{mediaId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "is_primary": true, "alt_text": "Side view", "position": 0 }

### Delete an image (the next one becomes primary if needed)
DELETE {{base}}/v1/companies/{{companyId}}/products/{{productId}}/images/{{mediaId}}

### Upload or replace the 3D model
PUT {{base}}/v1/companies/{{companyId}}/products/{{productId}}/model
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BOUNDARY

--BOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="chair.glb"
Content-Type: model/gltf-binary

< ./chair.glb
--BOUNDARY--

### Remove the model
DELETE {{base}}/v1/companies/{{companyId}}/products/{{productId}}/model

### Member download (works for drafts)
GET {{base}}/v1/companies/{{companyId}}/media/{{mediaId}}/file

### Public file (published products of active companies only)
GET {{base}}/v1/media/{{mediaId}}
